  "description": "WADREC crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C104 H90 Ce6 N4 O34 2+,2(C24 H21 Ce2 N4 O21 1-). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce1A (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce2A (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce3A (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 10 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 10 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.610-3.993 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.36-115.52°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C152H132Ce10N12O76. Article name explicitly identifies Ce(IV), Ce(III), Ce(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
